        <referenceFunction amount="1" category="transport systems" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="The inventory contains the work and materials for the installation of 1m2 of track bed. The information was modelled according to Messmer &amp; Frischknecht (2016) as listed in Tables 3.9 and 3.10 for concrete sleepers and converted to 1m2. The inventory includes the gravel for the superstructure as well as the gravel sand and geotextile for the substructure. It was assumed that the excavated material can be used for other purposes. The energy required for installation is included, as is the excavation work. According to SBB, gravel is transported by rail over 100km. The ecoinvent standard values were used for transport distances for material deliveries (Frischknecht et al., 2007). Land use (occupation, transfomration from and to) is taken into account in the superordinate inventory “Railway track, open field...”.&#10;&#10;The lifetime is around 60 years. Maintenance work, gravel cleaning and dismantling of the track bed are not taken into account.; UUID:07f579e1-e872-3f0f-84f4-b5e027cdaf9d" includedProcesses="The inventory includes all the materials, energy and transport necessary for constructing a railway track bed. Excluded are maintenance and disposal" infrastructureIncluded="true" infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="transport systems" localName="Track bed" localSubCategory="train\operations\infrastructure" name="Track bed" subCategory="train\operations\infrastructure" unit="m2a">
